218	1118,717,1292,953	Fig. 218.	The young pod of the checkerberry on its curved stalk, partly covered by the loose, pointed lobes of the calyx.
219	1396,677,1622,944	Fig. 219.	The ripe checkerberry cut lengthwise: the calyx grown thick and round, enclosing the small dry pod, whose cells show at the top.
220	22,1309,222,1702	220 Rose-hip.	A ripe rose-hip, oval like a small pear, crowned with the spreading lobes of the calyx, on a prickly stalk.
221	284,1235,565,1688	221 Rose-hip.	A rose-hip in flower cut lengthwise: the deep urn-shaped cup lined with pistils, their styles rising from its mouth among the stamens on the rim.
222	1268,1614,1628,1962	222. Young Strawberry.	A young strawberry at flowering time, cut lengthwise: a part of the calyx below and above it the rounded receptacle, its surface covered with little pistils.
